	Type	Description	Priority	Acceptance Criteria	Rationale	Comments
FR-001	Functional	The system shall allow an Emergency Requester to submit an emergency blood request specifying blood group, required units, emergency location, and urgency.	High	Pass if a valid emergency request is successfully recorded with all required details.	
The system needs accurate emergency request information to process the blood requirement.	Ensure all mandatory request fields are validated.
FR-002	Functional	The system shall check the current blood bank inventory for compatible blood units matching an emergency request.	High	Pass if the system displays the available compatible blood units and quantities for a valid request.	The system must determine whether the required blood is already available.	Inventory quantity should be updated after allocation.

FR-003	Functional	The system shall identify eligible donors with compatible blood groups within a 10 km radius when sufficient blood is unavailable.	High	Pass if only eligible donors with compatible blood groups within 10 km are selected.	Nearby compatible donors can help meet critical blood shortages quickly.	Donor eligibility and location must be verified.

FR-004	Functional	The system shall send emergency SMS notifications to compatible eligible donors identified by the donor matching process.	High	Pass if compatible donors receive the emergency notification within 30 seconds of the emergency flag.	Rapid notification is necessary during emergency blood shortages.	Notification delivery status should be recorded
FR-005	Functional	The system shall allow the Blood Bank Manager to add, update, allocate, and remove blood units while tracking their expiry dates.	High	Pass if inventory changes are accurately recorded and expired blood units cannot be allocated.	Accurate inventory management prevents incorrect allocation and use of expired blood.	Expiry date must be checked before allocation.



